      "text": "There's something deeply moving about the idea that the old world can still live within a modern country. Not because everything has remained unchanged, but because certain stories, traditions, and connections to the land can continue to mean something to new generations. I think that's what makes Scotland so fascinating. The past doesn't have to be perfectly preserved to remain part of people's lives. Sometimes its greatest legacy is how it continues to shape the present.",
